IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb2-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part VII (security certificates, registers
-- and transfers), section 48 -- INTERPRETATION AND GENERAL. Layer 1.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Every rule is named `<what it works out> within s <section>` and returns TRUE
-- when the facts it is given meet the provision. Each takes plain facts. Where a definition says
-- "includes", the rule is the listed cases or the ordinary meaning, which is a plain input. Part VII
-- has its own definitions (s 48(2)); where a word is also defined in s 2(1) (security, officer,
-- court) the rule here carries the section in its name, so the two cannot be confused.

§ `Part VII -- Security Certificates, Registers and Transfers`

§§ `s 48(1) Application of Part`

-- src:698 | 48 (1) The transfer or transmission of a security shall be governed by this Part.
@ref CBCA s 48(1) (src:698)
GIVEN `the matter is the transfer or transmission of a security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the matter is governed by Part VII within s 48(1)` MEANS
    `the matter is the transfer or transmission of a security`

§§ `s 48(2) Definitions`

-- "adverse claim includes ...": the two listed claims, or any claim that is one in the ordinary sense.
-- src:701 | adverse claim includes a claim that a transfer was or would be wrongful or that a particular adverse person is the owner of or has an interest or right in the security; (opposition)
@ref CBCA s 48(2) adverse claim (src:701)
GIVEN `the claim is that a transfer was or would be wrongful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is that a particular adverse person is the owner of the security or has an interest or right in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is an adverse claim in the ordinary sense` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`adverse claim within s 48(2)` MEANS
        `the claim is that a transfer was or would be wrongful`
    OR  `the claim is that a particular adverse person is the owner of the security or has an interest or right in it`
    OR  `the claim is an adverse claim in the ordinary sense`

-- "bearer": the person in possession of a security that is payable to bearer or is endorsed in blank.
-- src:702 | bearer means the person in possession of a security payable to bearer or endorsed in blank; (porteur)
@ref CBCA s 48(2) bearer (src:702)
GIVEN `the person is in possession of the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security is payable to bearer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security is endorsed in blank` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`bearer within s 48(2)` MEANS
        `the person is in possession of the security`
    AND (`the security is payable to bearer` OR `the security is endorsed in blank`)

-- "bona fide purchaser": a purchaser for value, in good faith and without notice of any adverse claim,
-- who takes delivery of (i) a security in bearer form or order form or (ii) a security in registered
-- form issued or endorsed to the purchaser or endorsed in blank.
-- src:703 | bona fide purchaser means a purchaser for value in good faith and without notice of any adverse claim who takes delivery of a security in bearer form or order form or of a security in registered form issued or endorsed to the purchaser or endorsed in blank; (acheteur de bonne foi)
@ref CBCA s 48(2) bona fide purchaser (src:703)
GIVEN `the person is a purchaser for value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is without notice of any adverse claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person takes delivery of the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form of the security taken` IS A `Form of a security`
      `the registered security was issued or endorsed to the purchaser or endorsed in blank` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`bona fide purchaser within s 48(2)` MEANS
        `the person is a purchaser for value`
    AND `the person acts in good faith`
    AND `the person is without notice of any adverse claim`
    AND `the person takes delivery of the security`
    AND (   `the form of the security taken` EQUALS `a security in bearer form`
         OR `the form of the security taken` EQUALS `a security in order form`
         OR (    `the form of the security taken` EQUALS `a security in registered form`
             AND `the registered security was issued or endorsed to the purchaser or endorsed in blank`))

-- "broker": engaged, exclusively or not, in the business of buying and selling securities, and who in
-- the transaction concerned acts for, or buys a security from, or sells a security to, a customer.
-- src:704 | broker means a person who is engaged, whether or not exclusively, in the business of buying and selling securities and who, in the transaction concerned, acts for, or buys a security from, or sells a security to a customer; (courtier)
@ref CBCA s 48(2) broker (src:704)
GIVEN `the person is engaged in the business of buying and selling securities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the transaction the person acts for a customer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the transaction the person buys a security from a customer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the transaction the person sells a security to a customer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`broker within s 48(2)` MEANS
        `the person is engaged in the business of buying and selling securities`
    AND (   `in the transaction the person acts for a customer`
         OR `in the transaction the person buys a security from a customer`
         OR `in the transaction the person sells a security to a customer`)

-- src:705 | delivery means voluntary transfer of possession; (livraison ou remise)
@ref CBCA s 48(2) delivery (src:705)
GIVEN `the transfer of possession is voluntary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`delivery within s 48(2)` MEANS
    `the transfer of possession is voluntary`

-- "fiduciary": any person who acts in a fiduciary capacity or as the administrator of the property of
-- others, and "includes" a personal representative of a deceased person.
-- src:706 | fiduciary means any person who acts in a fiduciary capacity or as the administrator of the property of others and includes a personal representative of a deceased person; (représentant)
@ref CBCA s 48(2) fiduciary (src:706)
GIVEN `the person acts in a fiduciary capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts as the administrator of the property of others` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a personal representative of a deceased person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`fiduciary within s 48(2)` MEANS
        `the person acts in a fiduciary capacity`
    OR  `the person acts as the administrator of the property of others`
    OR  `the person is a personal representative of a deceased person`

-- src:707 | fungible, in relation to securities, means securities of which any unit is, by nature or usage of trade, the equivalent of any other like unit; (fongibles)
@ref CBCA s 48(2) fungible (src:707)
GIVEN `any unit of the securities is by nature the equivalent of any other like unit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any unit of the securities is by usage of trade the equivalent of any other like unit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`fungible within s 48(2)` MEANS
        `any unit of the securities is by nature the equivalent of any other like unit`
    OR  `any unit of the securities is by usage of trade the equivalent of any other like unit`

-- src:708 | genuine means free of forgery or counterfeiting; (authentique)
@ref CBCA s 48(2) genuine (src:708)
GIVEN `the security is forged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security is counterfeit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`genuine within s 48(2)` MEANS
        (NOT `the security is forged`)
    AND (NOT `the security is counterfeit`)

-- src:709 | good faith means honesty in fact in the conduct of the transaction concerned; (bonne foi)
@ref CBCA s 48(2) good faith (src:709)
GIVEN `the person is honest in fact in the conduct of the transaction concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`good faith within s 48(2)` MEANS
    `the person is honest in fact in the conduct of the transaction concerned`

-- "holder": a person in possession of a security issued or endorsed to the person, or to the bearer, or
-- in blank.
-- src:710 | holder means a person in possession of a security issued or endorsed to the person or the bearer or in blank; (détenteur)
@ref CBCA s 48(2) holder (src:710)
GIVEN `the person is in possession of the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security is issued or endorsed to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security is issued or endorsed to the bearer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security is issued or endorsed in blank` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`holder within s 48(2)` MEANS
        `the person is in possession of the security`
    AND (   `the security is issued or endorsed to the person`
         OR `the security is issued or endorsed to the bearer`
         OR `the security is issued or endorsed in blank`)

-- "issuer includes a corporation": the three cases are listed, and "includes" leaves the ordinary
-- meaning (anyone who issues securities) as a plain input; fork F-P7-1 in NOTES.md.
-- src:711 | issuer includes a corporation
-- src:712 | (a) that is required by this Act to maintain a securities register,
-- src:713 | (b) that, in Quebec, issues securities that confer directly or indirectly rights in its property, or
-- src:714 | (c) that, elsewhere in Canada, directly or indirectly creates fractional interests in its rights or property and that issues securities as evidence of the fractional interests; (émetteur)
@ref CBCA s 48(2) issuer (src:711-714)
GIVEN `the person is an issuer in the ordinary sense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a corporation required by the Act to maintain a securities register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a corporation that in Quebec issues securities that confer directly or indirectly rights in its property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a corporation that elsewhere in Canada directly or indirectly creates fractional interests in its rights or property and issues securities as evidence of the fractional interests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`issuer within s 48(2)` MEANS
        `the person is an issuer in the ordinary sense`
    OR  `the person is a corporation required by the Act to maintain a securities register`
    OR  `the person is a corporation that in Quebec issues securities that confer directly or indirectly rights in its property`
    OR  `the person is a corporation that elsewhere in Canada directly or indirectly creates fractional interests in its rights or property and issues securities as evidence of the fractional interests`

-- "overissue": the issue of securities in excess of ANY maximum number the issuer is authorized by its
-- articles or by a trust indenture to issue. NOTHING for a maximum means that source sets none.
GIVEN `the number of securities issued` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the number issued is above a maximum that is stated, if there is one, within s 48(2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the maximum`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST limit THEN `the number of securities issued` GREATER THAN limit

-- src:715 | overissue means the issue of securities in excess of any maximum number of securities that the issuer is authorized by its articles or a trust indenture to issue; (émission excédentaire)
@ref CBCA s 48(2) overissue (src:715)
GIVEN `the number of securities issued` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum number the articles authorize the issuer to issue` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the maximum number a trust indenture authorizes the issuer to issue` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`overissue within s 48(2)` MEANS
        `the number issued is above a maximum that is stated, if there is one, within s 48(2)`
            `the number of securities issued` `the maximum number the articles authorize the issuer to issue`
    OR  `the number issued is above a maximum that is stated, if there is one, within s 48(2)`
            `the number of securities issued` `the maximum number a trust indenture authorizes the issuer to issue`

-- "purchaser": a person who takes an interest or right in a security by any voluntary transaction. A
-- way of taking that is not a voluntary transaction does not make a purchaser.
-- src:716 | purchaser means a person who takes an interest or right in a security by sale, mortgage, hypothec, pledge, issue, reissue, gift or any other voluntary transaction; (acquéreur)
@ref CBCA s 48(2) purchaser (src:716)
GIVEN `the way the person took the interest or right` IS A `Way of taking an interest in a security`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`purchaser within s 48(2)` MEANS
    NOT (`the way the person took the interest or right` EQUALS `taking an interest in a security in a way that is not a voluntary transaction`)

-- "security or security certificate": an instrument issued by a corporation that meets all four of (a)
-- to (d). Not the same as "security" in s 2(1) (src:68), which is the keel's `security within s 2(1)`.
-- src:717 | security or security certificate means an instrument issued by a corporation that is
-- src:718 | (a) in bearer, order or registered form,
-- src:719 | (b) of a type commonly dealt in on securities exchanges or markets or commonly recognized in any area in which it is issued or dealt in as a medium for investment,
-- src:720 | (c) one of a class or series or by its terms divisible into a class or series of instruments, and
-- src:721 | (d) evidence of a share, participation or other interest or right in or obligation of a corporation; (valeur mobilière ou certificat de valeur mobilière)
@ref CBCA s 48(2) security or security certificate (src:717-721)
GIVEN `the instrument is issued by a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is in bearer, order or registered form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is of a type commonly dealt in on securities exchanges or markets or commonly recognized as a medium for investment in the area where it is issued or dealt in` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is one of a class or series or by its terms divisible into a class or series of instruments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is evidence of a share, participation or other interest or right in or obligation of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`security or security certificate within s 48(2)` MEANS
        `the instrument is issued by a corporation`
    AND `the instrument is in bearer, order or registered form`
    AND `the instrument is of a type commonly dealt in on securities exchanges or markets or commonly recognized as a medium for investment in the area where it is issued or dealt in`
    AND `the instrument is one of a class or series or by its terms divisible into a class or series of instruments`
    AND `the instrument is evidence of a share, participation or other interest or right in or obligation of a corporation`

-- "transfer includes transmission by operation of law".
-- src:722 | transfer includes transmission by operation of law; (transfert)
@ref CBCA s 48(2) transfer (src:722)
GIVEN `the dealing is a transfer in the ordinary sense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dealing is a transmission by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`transfer within s 48(2)` MEANS
        `the dealing is a transfer in the ordinary sense`
    OR  `the dealing is a transmission by operation of law`

-- "trust indenture" in s 48(2) (line 723 of the text) says only "a trust indenture as defined in section
-- 82"; the rule is `trust indenture within s 82(1)` in cb2-part8-trust-indentures.l4 and is not written
-- twice.

-- "unauthorized", of a signature or an endorsement: made without actual, implied or apparent
-- authority, and "includes" a forgery.
-- src:724 | unauthorized, in relation to a signature or an endorsement, means one made without actual, implied or apparent authority and includes a forgery; (non autorisé)
@ref CBCA s 48(2) unauthorized (src:724)
GIVEN `the signature or endorsement was made with actual authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signature or endorsement was made with implied authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signature or endorsement was made with apparent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signature or endorsement is a forgery` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`unauthorized within s 48(2)` MEANS
        `the signature or endorsement is a forgery`
    OR  (    (NOT `the signature or endorsement was made with actual authority`)
         AND (NOT `the signature or endorsement was made with implied authority`)
         AND (NOT `the signature or endorsement was made with apparent authority`))

-- "valid": issued in accordance with the applicable law AND the articles of the issuer, or validated
-- under section 52 (overissue; the rules for s 52 are in cb2-part7-registers.l4).
-- src:725 | valid means issued in accordance with the applicable law and the articles of the issuer, or validated under section 52. (valide)
@ref CBCA s 48(2) valid (src:725)
GIVEN `the security was issued in accordance with the applicable law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security was issued in accordance with the articles of the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security was validated under section 52` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`valid within s 48(2)` MEANS
        (    `the security was issued in accordance with the applicable law`
         AND `the security was issued in accordance with the articles of the issuer`)
    OR  `the security was validated under section 52`

§§ `s 48(3) Negotiable instruments`

-- A security is a negotiable instrument, except where its transfer is restricted and the restriction is
-- noted on it in accordance with s 49(8) (the restriction is noted conspicuously on the certificate).
-- src:726 | Negotiable instruments
-- src:727 | (3) Except where its transfer is restricted and noted on a security in accordance with subsection 49(8), a security is a negotiable instrument.
@ref CBCA s 48(3) (src:726-727)
GIVEN `the transfer of the security is restricted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the restriction is noted on the security in accordance with subsection 49(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a security is a negotiable instrument within s 48(3)` MEANS
    NOT (    `the transfer of the security is restricted`
         AND `the restriction is noted on the security in accordance with subsection 49(8)`)

§§ `s 48(4) Registered form`

-- src:728 | Registered form
-- src:729 | (4) A security is in registered form if
-- src:730 | (a) it specifies a person entitled to the security or to the rights it evidences, and its transfer is capable of being recorded in a securities register; or
-- src:731 | (b) it bears a statement that it is in registered form.
@ref CBCA s 48(4) (src:728-731)
GIVEN `the security specifies a person entitled to the security or to the rights it evidences` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer of the security is capable of being recorded in a securities register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security bears a statement that it is in registered form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a security is in registered form within s 48(4)` MEANS
        (    `the security specifies a person entitled to the security or to the rights it evidences`
         AND `the transfer of the security is capable of being recorded in a securities register`)
    OR  `the security bears a statement that it is in registered form`

§§ `s 48(5) Order form`

-- src:732 | Order form
-- src:733 | (5) A debt obligation is in order form where, by its terms, it is payable to the order or assigns of any person therein specified with reasonable certainty or to that person’s order.
@ref CBCA s 48(5) (src:732-733)
GIVEN `the security is a debt obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by its terms it is payable to the order or assigns of a person specified in it with reasonable certainty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by its terms it is payable to the order of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a debt obligation is in order form within s 48(5)` MEANS
        `the security is a debt obligation`
    AND (   `by its terms it is payable to the order or assigns of a person specified in it with reasonable certainty`
         OR `by its terms it is payable to the order of that person`)

§§ `s 48(6) Bearer form`

-- src:734 | Bearer form
-- src:735 | (6) A security is in bearer form if it is payable to bearer according to its terms and not by reason of any endorsement.
@ref CBCA s 48(6) (src:734-735)
GIVEN `according to its terms the security is payable to bearer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is payable to bearer only by reason of an endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a security is in bearer form within s 48(6)` MEANS
        `according to its terms the security is payable to bearer`
    AND (NOT `it is payable to bearer only by reason of an endorsement`)

§§ `s 48(7) Guarantor for issuer`

-- A guarantor for an issuer is deemed to be an issuer to the extent of the guarantee, whether or not
-- the obligation is noted on the security. Whether it is noted makes no difference, so no input asks.
-- src:736 | Guarantor for issuer
-- src:737 | (7) A guarantor for an issuer is deemed to be an issuer to the extent of the guarantee whether or not the obligation is noted on the security.
@ref CBCA s 48(7) (src:736-737)
GIVEN `the person is a guarantor for an issuer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a guarantor is deemed to be an issuer to the extent of the guarantee within s 48(7)` MEANS
    `the person is a guarantor for an issuer`

§§ `s 48(4) to (6) The forms a security takes`

-- The three forms are defined separately and the text does not say that a security cannot be in more
-- than one; this rule lists every form the facts make out, and the named constructor
-- `a security in none of the three forms in section 48` when it is in none (fork F-P7-2 in NOTES.md).
-- src:728 | Registered form
-- src:729 | (4) A security is in registered form if
-- src:730 | (a) it specifies a person entitled to the security or to the rights it evidences, and its transfer is capable of being recorded in a securities register; or
-- src:731 | (b) it bears a statement that it is in registered form.
-- src:732 | Order form
-- src:733 | (5) A debt obligation is in order form where, by its terms, it is payable to the order or assigns of any person therein specified with reasonable certainty or to that person’s order.
-- src:734 | Bearer form
-- src:735 | (6) A security is in bearer form if it is payable to bearer according to its terms and not by reason of any endorsement.
@ref CBCA s 48(4) to (6) (src:728-735)
GIVEN `the security is in registered form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debt obligation is in order form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security is in bearer form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Form of a security`
`the forms of a security within s 48(4) to (6)` MEANS
    IF NOT (   `the security is in registered form`
            OR `the debt obligation is in order form`
            OR `the security is in bearer form`)
    THEN LIST `a security in none of the three forms in section 48`
    ELSE append `the registered form, if any` (append `the order form, if any` `the bearer form, if any`)
    WHERE
        `the registered form, if any` MEANS
            IF `the security is in registered form` THEN LIST `a security in registered form` ELSE EMPTY
        `the order form, if any` MEANS
            IF `the debt obligation is in order form` THEN LIST `a security in order form` ELSE EMPTY
        `the bearer form, if any` MEANS
            IF `the security is in bearer form` THEN LIST `a security in bearer form` ELSE EMPTY
